<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog https://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">
    <!--
        The first-login notice stops being a row this release. Its wording is now the setup screen in
        the webapp, and consent_decision.notice_version points at the release that published it.

        This is the compatibility half of the removal, so it drops nothing
        (docs/contributor/database-migration.mdx § Changelog immutability policy). consent_notice and
        the digests already in consent_decision stay exactly as they are, which keeps the previous
        release bootable against this schema — it still reads the archive on every consent request —
        and keeps rolling back the application image an option. The next release drops both; until it
        does, the object exclusions in application/build.gradle.kts keep the drift gate quiet.
    -->
    <changeSet id="1789067582535-1" author="hephaestus">
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="consent_decision" columnName="notice_sha256" columnDataType="varchar(64)"/>
        <rollback>
            <stop>Restoring NOT NULL fails once a decision has been recorded without a digest, and the ledger is append-only, so there is nothing to backfill with. Restore a pre-upgrade database backup.</stop>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
    <!--
        The append-only guard compares every column erasure may not change, and `=` on two NULLs is
        NULL rather than true. Without this the guard rejects the one UPDATE it exists to permit —
        clearing account_id — for every decision recorded from this release on.
    -->
    <changeSet id="1789067582535-2" author="hephaestus">
        <sql splitStatements="false"><![CDATA[
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.enforce_consent_decision_append_only() RETURNS trigger
    LANGUAGE plpgsql
    AS $$
            BEGIN
                IF TG_OP = 'UPDATE'
                   AND OLD.account_id IS NOT NULL AND NEW.account_id IS NULL
                   AND OLD.id = NEW.id
                   AND OLD.purpose = NEW.purpose
                   AND OLD.granted = NEW.granted
                   AND OLD.mechanism = NEW.mechanism
                   AND OLD.notice_version = NEW.notice_version
                   AND OLD.notice_sha256 IS NOT DISTINCT FROM NEW.notice_sha256
                   AND OLD.occurred_at = NEW.occurred_at THEN
                    RETURN NEW;
                END IF;
                RAISE EXCEPTION 'consent_decision is append-only';
            END;
            $$;
]]></sql>
        <!--
            Refused rather than reversed. Liquibase rolls back in reverse order, so restoring the
            null-unsafe comparison here would commit before the NOT NULL above fails on the rows this
            release allowed, leaving a database whose erasure path rejects exactly those rows.
        -->
        <rollback>
            <stop>Rolling this back would restore a guard that refuses to erase the account reference on any decision recorded without a digest. Restore a pre-upgrade database backup.</stop>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
